      "source_url": "https://adkhighpeaksfoundation.org/mt-adams/"
    },
    {
      "year": 2011,
      "event": "other",
      "note": "spring 2011 flooding destroyed the steel cable bridge over the Hudson River, forcing volunteers to ford the river",
      "from": "research",
      "source_url": "https://adkhighpeaksfoundation.org/mt-adams/"
    },
    {
      "year": 2011,
      "event": "restored",
      "note": "A new wind-resistant roof, built off site, was helicoptered in with DEC support and installed in summer 2011 under the ADK High Peaks Foundation project; footing repairs followed.",
      "from": "nysffla_projects",
      "source_url": "https://www.nysffla.org/Newsletters/2017/2017-07.pdf"
    },
    {
      "year": 2013,
      "event": "restored",
      "note": "The ADK High Peaks Foundation's restoration of the tower (roof, footings, windows, maps, paint) was completed in 2013.",
      "from": "nysffla_projects",
      "source_url": "https://www.nysffla.org/Newsletters/2017/2017-07.pdf"
    },
    {
      "year": 2017,
      "event": "closed",
      "note": "DEC advised the public to avoid the tower after ice and wind damaged its top landing, pending repairs planned for later in 2017 (reported March 2017).",
      "from": "nysffla_projects",
      "source_url": "https://www.nysffla.org/Newsletters/2017/2017-03.pdf"
    },
    {
      "year": 2017,
      "event": "restored",
      "note": "A volunteer from the Mount Adams crew replaced and repaired the tower's safety netting on May 13, 2017.",
